<title>INDIA: India's Hindalco 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's Hindalco 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		3,909.55   vs    4,011.46</p>
<p>    Net sales		11,570.77   vs   12,518.07</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	    52.50   vs	 80.79</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	     4.5    vs	  4.0</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	    5,527.71   vs    6,759.82</p>
<p>    Depreciation		423.16   vs	348.36</p>
<p>    Tax			 1,195.00   vs    2,400.00</p>
<p>    Exports		   1,566.00   vs    1,055.00</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Production Data  (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    Aluminium Metal     166,272	vs  175,398</p>
<p>    Rolled Products	18,302	vs   31,378</p>
<p>    Extrusion		11,798	vs   12,589</p>
<p>Note: Hindalco Industries Ltd said it has planned investments in excess of 17.50 billion rupees towards its expansion and modernisation project since 1994. It said capital expenditure incurred during the year was 5.75 billion rupees.</p>
<p>India's largest private aluminium maker said earnings per share for the current year were on an enlarged equity capital after the issue of bonus equity shares last May.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
